{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The run finished green, but it did not meet the requirement.",
      "",
      "- **Pipeline green:** The workflow summary shows build-test-and-deploy SUCCESS, with all three jobs passing.",
      "- **Behaviour correct:** The run was on branch `koans-08-branch-filters`, not `production`. Yet `deploy` ran and succeeded, which violates the rule that `deploy` runs only for `production` commits.",
      "- **Why it happened:** The workflow entry for `deploy` has only `requires: [test-production]` and no branch filter. `requires` only orders jobs; it does not restrict branches. So `deploy` runs on every branch where its upstream jobs pass.",
      "- **Fix:** Add `filters: branches: only: production` to the `deploy` entry under `workflows.build-test-and-deploy.jobs`.",
      "- **Why not the alternatives:** An ignore-list cannot enumerate every non-production branch. Filters are not valid on the job definition itself. Relying on `requires` does not restrict branches. `build` and `test-production` have no restriction and still run on `production`, so the workflow there stays green."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
