{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy ran on untagged branch push",
    "Explanation": [
      "The run passed, but it did the wrong thing.",
      "",
      "**What happened:** All three jobs (build, test, deploy) succeeded, so the workflow is green. The run was triggered on the branch `koans-09-tag-filters` with no tag shown. The config has no filters, so `deploy` ran on an untagged branch push. The requirement forbids that, so the behaviour is incorrect.",
      "",
      "**Why only `deploy` is not enough:** By default, CircleCI does not run jobs for tag pushes. A job only runs for a tag if it has an explicit `filters.tags` setting. Also, if a job `requires` other jobs, it can only run when those upstream jobs also run for the tag.",
      "",
      "**Fix:** Change the workflow configuration of all jobs:",
      "- **build** and **test**: add `filters: tags: only: /^beta-.*/` so they run when `beta-main-0.1.1` is pushed.",
      "- **deploy**: add the same beta-only tag filter, plus `filters: branches: ignore: /.*/` so it never runs on branch pushes.",
      "",
      "With this, `beta-*` tags produce a green workflow that deploys. `alpha-*` tags trigger nothing. Untagged branch pushes still run build and test but skip deploy. Allowing all tags would wrongly let `alpha-*` tags deploy."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
